# class: glossary
# schema: term | definition | source
# source: docs/architecture.md
# recipe: builtin:architecture

slot | (service, environment) cell in the deployment matrix; latest deployment is the slot's current state | @docs/architecture.md#api-contract
current | The slot's most recent deployment event (any status) | @docs/architecture.md#api-contract
lastSuccessful | Most recent successful deployment for a slot; null when current.status==success or no prior success | @docs/architecture.md#api-contract
previousFailed | true when current.status==in-progress and the most recent terminal deployment was a failure | @docs/architecture.md#api-contract
matrix | services x environments grid; one row per service; latest deployment per slot | @docs/architecture.md#7-target-architecture
Write surface | Endpoint group library exposing POST /api/deployments + fetcher-state endpoints; X-Api-Key gated | @docs/architecture.md#dashboard-backend--write-and-read-surfaces
Read surface | Endpoint group library exposing matrix, history, discovery, SSE, health; unauthenticated | @docs/architecture.md#dashboard-backend--write-and-read-surfaces
App Gateway | nginx reverse proxy; sole public ingress; path+method routing matrix; SSE pass-through tuned | @docs/architecture.md#app-gateway
Real-time Hub | API-instance-level LISTEN on Postgres deployments channel; per-instance SSE fan-out | @docs/architecture.md#components
deployments table | Append-only Postgres table; source of truth for matrix + history + lastSuccessful/previousFailed derivation; gains nullable progress_reporter column per CR-0009 | @docs/architecture.md#data-model
LISTEN/NOTIFY | Postgres pub/sub mechanism powering cross-instance SSE fan-out without sticky sessions | @docs/architecture.md#7-target-architecture
SSE | text/event-stream HTTP-1.1 protocol; browser-native EventSource; supports Last-Event-ID | @docs/architecture.md#api-contract
HISTORY_RETENTION_DAYS | Env-var; default 365; daily pruning job deletes rows older than threshold | @docs/architecture.md#data-model
API_TOKEN | Env-var on API container; expected value of X-Api-Key on write-group endpoints | @docs/architecture.md#infrastructure
ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection | Env-var; Postgres connection string consumed by API container | @docs/architecture.md#infrastructure
View | UX axis: Detailed / Compact / Glance / Focus (CR-0002) | @docs/cr/CR-0002-four-named-views-and-attribute-picker.md
Layout | UX axis: Matrix (Phase 2 per CR-0007) / Swim-lane (default) / Workflow-rows (CR-0003) | @docs/cr/CR-0003-tree-topology-and-layout-axis.md
Theme | UX axis: light / dark / auto; localStorage-persisted; FOIT-safe bootstrap (CR-0006 + ADR-0003) | @docs/cr/CR-0006-light-dark-auto-theme.md
correlationAttribute | Per-request query parameter resolving topology correlation attribute (CR-0003 + ADR-0001) | @docs/adr/ADR-0001-topology-derivation-five-pass.md
topology.edges | Per-service array of {from, to, source: explicit|correlated} edges (CR-0003) | @docs/adr/ADR-0001-topology-derivation-five-pass.md
deployment_id | CR-0003 required ingest field; CI/CD-side identifier; used by parent_deployments for explicit edges | @docs/cr/CR-0003-tree-topology-and-layout-axis.md
parent_deployments | CR-0003 optional ingest field; list of parent deployment_id strings (same service) | @docs/cr/CR-0003-tree-topology-and-layout-axis.md
ref | CR-0004 optional payload field; git ref string | @docs/cr/CR-0004-ref-and-sha-optional-fields.md
sha | CR-0004 optional payload field; git commit sha | @docs/cr/CR-0004-ref-and-sha-optional-fields.md
NFR-09 reflow invariant | Layout must reflow under any (services x envs x name-len x version-len x viewport) combo without overlap; CSS Grid + ResizeObserver enforcement | @docs/architecture.md#5-non-functional-requirements
ProblemDetails | RFC-7807 error response format adopted across all endpoints (CR-0008) | @docs/cr/CR-0008-api-validation-and-openapi-scalar.md
Scalar | OpenAPI documentation UI replacing Swagger UI (CR-0008) | @docs/cr/CR-0008-api-validation-and-openapi-scalar.md
X-Progress-Reporter | CR-0009 universal pusher-attribution request header; ≤ 64 chars non-whitespace; optional on POST /api/deployments, required on GET/PUT /api/fetcher/state/{source-id}; persisted on event row; ValidationProblemDetails errors-map key uses wire-literal name | @docs/architecture.md#api-contract
progress_reporter | CR-0009 nullable VARCHAR(64) column on events/deployments table; persists X-Progress-Reporter header value; surfaced on DeploymentEventResponse + CurrentDeployment + LastSuccessfulDeployment Read DTOs | @docs/architecture.md#dashboardfetcher-optional-pull-mode-adapter
Dashboard.Fetcher | CR-0009 optional out-of-process pull-mode adapter; .NET Worker; polls CI/CD API on interval; pushes via POST /api/deployments with X-Progress-Reporter; backend behaves identically whether deployed or not | @docs/architecture.md#dashboardfetcher-optional-pull-mode-adapter
Dashboard.Fetcher.Host | CR-0009 host project at backend/fetcher-host/; ASP.NET Core Worker (Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Worker); composition root + env-var config | @docs/architecture.md#dashboardfetcher-optional-pull-mode-adapter
fetcher_state | CR-0009 new table; PK (progress_reporter, source_id); cursor VARCHAR(4096) NOT NULL; updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL; backend-held cursor per ADR-0004 Decision 1 | @docs/architecture.md#api-contract
ICiCdAdapter | ADR-0004 Decision 4 plug-in interface; AdapterId + FetchPageAsync(sourceId, opaqueCursor, pageSize, ct) -> (events, newCursor, hasMore); one impl per CI/CD tool | @docs/architecture.md#dashboardfetcher-optional-pull-mode-adapter
INITIAL_FETCH_LIMIT | CR-0009 env-var; first-fetch cap when no cursor exists; default 50, ceiling 500 | @docs/architecture.md#dashboardfetcher-optional-pull-mode-adapter
source-id | CR-0009 per-fetcher logical scope (e.g. owner/repo); path parameter on fetcher-state endpoints; cursor keyed by (progress_reporter, source_id) | @docs/architecture.md#api-contract